An accepted socket is blocking on Radix

A socket that accept(2) returns does not take O_NONBLOCK from the
listening socket on Radix, as on Linux, and unlike the BSDs. PHP copies
the listening stream's record of it to the new stream on every system but
Linux, in both of its TCP transports: the plain one, and OpenSSL's, which
takes tcp:// as well when the openssl extension is built in, as it is
here. A server that made its listening socket non-blocking got accepted
streams it took for non-blocking that were not: their reads waited for
data with no timeout, and stream_set_blocking(false) did nothing, as the
stream said it was so already. PHP's test of this,
ext/standard/tests/streams/gh8472.phpt, hung there.

diff --git a/ext/openssl/xp_ssl.c b/ext/openssl/xp_ssl.c
index d5425f98..dcabe260 100644
--- a/ext/openssl/xp_ssl.c
+++ b/ext/openssl/xp_ssl.c
@@ -2287,8 +2287,8 @@ static inline int php_openssl_tcp_sockop_accept(php_stream *stream, php_openssl_
 		memcpy(clisockdata, sock, sizeof(clisockdata->s));
 
 		clisockdata->s.socket = clisock;
-#ifdef __linux__
-		/* O_NONBLOCK is not inherited on Linux */
+#if defined(__linux__) || defined(__radix__)
+		/* O_NONBLOCK is not inherited on Linux or Radix */
 		clisockdata->s.is_blocked = true;
 #endif
 
diff --git a/main/streams/xp_socket.c b/main/streams/xp_socket.c
index ac419493..ab6c50df 100644
--- a/main/streams/xp_socket.c
+++ b/main/streams/xp_socket.c
@@ -883,8 +883,8 @@ static inline int php_tcp_sockop_accept(php_stream *stream, php_netstream_data_t
 
 		memcpy(clisockdata, sock, sizeof(*clisockdata));
 		clisockdata->socket = clisock;
-#ifdef __linux__
-		/* O_NONBLOCK is not inherited on Linux */
+#if defined(__linux__) || defined(__radix__)
+		/* O_NONBLOCK is not inherited on Linux or Radix */
 		clisockdata->is_blocked = true;
 #endif
 
